  "policy": [
    "Every capital and registered project district owns one bounded terrain-owned ground transition.",
    "Wide-area close terrain is camera-streamed; local site overlays contain only material-matched foundation contact.",
    "Every site alpha is a subset of the registered land alpha and cannot cover the locked water layer.",
    "Static shore geometry and material remain land-owned; persistent swash and wet-edge motion remain water-owned.",
    "Ground-only material contacts support structures without redrawing geography or defining infrastructure.",
    "NinjaOne project contacts are distributed across territory-owned anchors rather than compressed inside the capital envelope.",
    "Vegetation, actors, labels, and transient effects remain in their later owning phases."
  ]
